1. CONVENTIONS
==============

  Detectors        H1, L1, V1 (fixed order everywhere; a missing detector is
                   unit white noise, asd_bands 0)
  Sampling         4096 Hz, 4 s window = 16384 samples per detector
  Band             20 Hz (f_lower) to 1024 Hz for features; whitening to Nyquist
  Whitening        h_w(f) = h(f) / sqrt(PSD(f) / (4 df)): unit-variance noise,
                   so absolute amplitude carries distance and SNR
  Reference epoch  every simulated event sits at GPS_REF = 1369224018 (window
                   centre); antenna patterns and sky rotation use this epoch
  Merger time      geocent_time = merger offset from the window centre [s],
                   drawn in [-1.5, +1.5]
  Masses           detector frame, mass_1 >= mass_2 always
  Spins            aligned spin magnitudes a1, a2
  Parameters       mass_1, mass_2, luminosity_distance, ra, dec, theta_jn,
  (fixed order)    psi, phase, geocent_time, a1, a2
  Rank             signals in a window are ordered by the loudness proxy
                   Mc^(5/6) / d_L; rank 0 = loudest. The same ordering is used
                   when building data, when remixing and at inference
  Network SNR      for whitened data, the optimal SNR is the L2 norm of the
                   whitened signal (summed over kept detectors)


