3. DATA GENERATION — src/ahsd/data/
===================================

3.1 Populations (parameter_sampler.py + configs)

  Class   Fraction   Masses (M☉)                        Spins            Distance (Mpc)   Waveform
  ─────   ────────   ────────────────────────────────   ──────────────   ──────────────   ─────────────────────
  BBH     0.65       m1, m2 log-flat in [5, 100]        a1, a2 ≤ 0.99    100 – 4000       IMRPhenomXP
  NSBH    0.15       BH log-flat [3, 100], NS [1, 2.5]  BH ≤ 0.9,        20 – 1200        IMRPhenomNSBH
                                                        NS ≤ 0.05
  BNS     0.15       uniform [1, 2.5]                   a1, a2 ≤ 0.05    10 – 400         IMRPhenomD_NRTidalv2
  noise   0.05       — (noise-only window, no signal)

  Fractions are for the mixed dataset (data_config_fixed.yaml). The class
  datasets (data_config_{bbh,nsbh,bns}_v3.yaml) put 0.95 on one class and
  0.05 on noise.

  All classes: distance uniform in d_L within the class range (the
  distance_prior is stored with the dataset so posteriors can be reweighted
  to a d_L^2 prior at inference); ra uniform; dec = arcsin(U[-1,1]);
  theta_jn = arccos(U[-1,1]); psi U[0, π); phase U[0, 2π); geocent_time
  U[-1.5, 1.5] s.

  NSBH black-hole spin is capped at 0.9: IMRPhenomNSBH produces a long
  unphysical post-merger tail for spins ≥ 0.94 at mass ratios above ~20.

3.2 Events (dataset_generator.py)

  - With probability overlap_fraction = 0.3 an event holds 2–4 signals, each
    an independent real source (any class in the configured mix), each with
    its own merger time in the window. Otherwise one signal (or noise only).
  - Noise: Gaussian, coloured by the design PSD of each detector, with an
    independent 63-bit seed per event.
  - SNR gate: the event is kept if the primary signal's network SNR ≥
    min_snr = 6; secondary signals may be quieter.
  - Splits: train 0.8 / validation 0.1 / test 0.1.

3.3 Waveforms (bilby_pipeline.py)

  BilbyWaveformGenerator chooses one of two paths per signal:

  fits_window(p):  1.2·τ(20 Hz) + 0.25 s ≤ T/2 + t_c
                   (τ = leading-order chirp time from 20 Hz to merger)

  short path       frequency-domain generation over the 4 s window, projected
                   with bilby interferometers, whitened in the window.
  long path        (all BNS and NSBH, light BBH) generate_long():
                   the waveform starts PRE_ROLL = 8 s before the window at
                   f_start = min(f_ref, max(20 Hz, f(τ = T/2 + t_c + 8 s))),
                   over a power-of-two duration D that holds the inspiral, the
                   window and POST = 2 s after it. The long series is
                   projected, whitened as a whole, then cropped to the window,
                   so the window holds the true last seconds before merger —
                   the same order of operations as real data (whiten a long
                   segment, then crop).

  BilbySignalInjector projects onto each detector (antenna patterns and
  light-travel delays at GPS_REF). BilbyPreprocessor whitens with the design
  PSD of each detector. Interferometer objects are cached per detector.

3.4 Storage

  Each event stores, per detector: whitened noise and each whitened signal
  component separately (float16), plus the 11 labels per signal. The total
  strain is never stored; it is rebuilt by summing components.

  generate_parallel.py   N independent shards (one seed each, one per CPU),
                         merged into one dataset with relative split
                         symlinks; writes dataset_config.yaml and
                         generation_manifest.json
  build_memmap_cache     per split, data/<ds>/memmap/<split>/:
                           signals.npy  [M, 3, 16384] float16  every signal
                           params.npy   [M, 11]       float32  its labels
                           noise.npy    [N, 3, 16384] float16  noise pool
                           events.json  [(start, n_signals), ...] per event


4. DATASET AUDIT — scripts/audit_dataset.py
===========================================

  Run on every dataset before training; exit code ≠ 0 on any hard failure,
  so SLURM jobs chained with afterok only train on clean data.

  Structure      event index covers every signal exactly once, contiguous
  Physics        all labels finite; mass_1 ≥ mass_2; angles and spins in range;
                 distance inside the model's support (--dist-range)
  Population     classes present/absent exactly as configured; distance inside
                 the per-class range; no empty distance decile; overlap
                 fraction near the config value
  Signals        finite; no all-zero waveforms; no float16 saturation;
                 loudest signal per event ≥ min_snr;
                 post-merger energy: < 1% of a signal's energy may lie more
                 than 0.5 s after merger (correct signals: ~1e-5, heavy BBH
                 ≤ 5e-3 from whitening ringing at 20 Hz; an inspiral folded
                 into the window or a waveform-model breakdown: 1e-2 – 0.5)
  Noise          finite; whitened std ≈ 1; no near-silent segments
  Duplicates     exact (hash) checks on parameter sets and noise segments


5. REMIXING — experiments/remix_data.py
=======================================

  RemixDataset builds a fresh training example from the stored components
  each epoch. Two RNG streams per epoch slot: rng_sig (signal identity) and
  rng_noise (noise realization), seeded by (seed, epoch, slot). The trainer
  calls set_epoch() every epoch; persistent_workers must stay False so the
  workers receive it.

  Per event, in order:

  Step                Mechanism                                       Labels
  ─────────────────   ─────────────────────────────────────────────   ─────────────────────────
  noise               p = real_noise_prob (0.9): real detector noise   —
                      crop; otherwise a random stored Gaussian
                      realization
  sky remap           p = delay_aug (0.5) per signal, delay_aug.py:    ra, dec, psi relabelled
                      a new sky chosen among 64 candidates with the
                      closest antenna response; per-detector delays
                      applied exactly (FFT phase ramp); psi rotated
                      in closed form
  distance rescale    amplitude × s, s ~ U[0.75, 1.33]; skipped if     d_L ÷ s
                      d_L ÷ s leaves the model's distance support
  time shift          common circular roll ≤ ±0.1 s (signals with      geocent_time += Δt
                      |t_c| < 1.45 s)
  overlap sum         components summed                                —
  re-colouring        real-noise events: the summed signal is moved   —
                      into the segment's whitening,
                      irfft(rfft(sig) · ASD_design / ASD_measured)
                      (exact: whitening is diagonal in frequency;
                      filter clamped at 50)
  detector dropout    p = det_dropout (0.2): keep a random detector    —
                      subset; dropped detectors get fresh noise
  re-sort             signals re-ordered by Mc^(5/6)/d_L after         rank labels consistent
                      rescaling

  Output per event: (strain [3,16384], params [5,11] by rank, n_signals,
  network SNR, asd_bands [3,16]).

  asd_bands         per detector, band-mean of log(design_ASD/measured_ASD)
                    over 16 log bands from 20 Hz to Nyquist; 0 for Gaussian
                    noise and dropped detectors. Tells the model how sensitive
                    each detector was, so whitened amplitude maps to distance.

  Real-noise bank   scripts/download_gwosc_noise_bank.py → data/noise_bank/:
                    64 s GWOSC segments per detector from O1–O4 (Virgo from
                    O2 on), each whitened by its own measured PSD (gwpy) and
                    stored with its ASD on the 4 s rfft grid. Crops are taken
                    at random positions, with a random time-reversal and sign
                    flip.


6. MODEL — src/ahsd/models/
===========================

6.1 Overview (LeanNPE, lean_npe.py; encoder = CoherentEncoder)

  strain [B, 3, 16384]  (NaN → 0, clamped to ±100)
     │
     ├─ energy branch ──── 16 windows × 3 det: log mean-square of RAW strain
     │                      MLP 48 → 64 → 64                           [B, 64]
     │
     ├─ conv stem ──────── asinh(strain), per detector, shared weights:
     │                      Conv1d(1→32, k64, s8) GELU
     │                      Conv1d(32→64, k16, s4) GELU
     │                      Conv1d(64→128, k8, s4) GELU
     │                      Conv1d(128→192, k4, s2) GELU
     │                      → 61 tokens/det + sinusoidal position
     │                        + detector embedding → 183 tokens × 192
     │
     ├─ geometry branch ── 201 features → MLP 128 → 4 tokens            (6.2)
     ├─ MF branch ──────── 3 × K × 4 features → MLP 256 → 128 → 4 tokens,
     │  (--mf_tokens)       gated and added into the geometry tokens    (6.3)
     ├─ polarization ───── 15 features → LayerNorm → 128 → 128 → 2 tokens
     │  (--pol_features)                                                 (6.4)
     │
     ▼
  [4 (+2) conditioning tokens | 183 conv tokens]
     → transformer: 3 pre-norm layers, d = 192, 6 heads, FFN 768, dropout 0.05
     → attention pooling with 8 learned queries                     [B, 1536]
     │
     ├─ PSD branch ─────── asd_bands [3 × 16] → MLP 64 → 32            [B, 32]
     ▼
  concat [1536 + 64 + 32] → Linear 512 → GELU → Linear 256 = context [B, 256]
     │
     ⊕ rank embedding (32, up to 5 signals)                           [B, 288]
     ▼
  neural spline flow (6.5) → 11-D posterior in [-1, 1] → ParamScaler → physical

  Amplitude is never normalized away: the stem sees asinh-compressed strain
  (monotone, bounded), the energy branch reads the raw strain, and the PSD
  branch supplies detector sensitivity.

6.2 Geometry branch (CoherentEncoder._geometry_rel)

  From d_d(f) = rfft(x_d) (orthonormal) over 20–1024 Hz, 16 log-spaced bands:

  log band energy             per detector × band                       48
  power-weighted coherence    per pair: γ = Σ d_i d_j* / Σ |d_i||d_j|,
                              as |γ|, cos φ, sin φ per band             144
  arrival-time delay          per pair: power-weighted mean of the
                              cross-spectrum phase increment over 4 Hz
                              (group delay, immune to the constant
                              polarization phase) + its concentration    6
  log amplitude ratio         per pair                                    3
                                                                       ────
                                                                        201

  Tokens are dropped per sample with probability geom_dropout (0.25) during
  training, so the conv path stays self-sufficient.

6.3 Matched-filter (MF) tokens (CoherentEncoder._mf_features)

  A fixed bank of unit-norm whitened templates per detector,
  assets/mf_bank_*.npz (built by build_mf_bank.py):

    mf_bank_bbh.npz    164 templates, 26 chirp masses 4.2–90 M☉ × q grid
                       {0.06 … 1}, IMRPhenomXP     (BBH and mixed models)
    mf_bank_nsbh.npz   124 templates               (built, not used)
    mf_bank_bns.npz     92 templates               (built, not used)
    mf_bank.npz        original bank, Mc 12–45     (default for old checkpoints)

  For each (detector, template) the complex overlap series is computed by an
  inverse FFT over only the 4016 in-band bins: an alias-free baseband series
  at ~1 ms resolution. Within ±1.6 s of the window centre the peak gives four
  channels: asinh(|z|) in SNR units, cos and sin of the phase at the peak
  (heterodyne ramp restored), and the peak time. The |z| pattern across the
  grid is a profile likelihood over (Mc, q): the chirp-phase mass statistic
  the conv stem cannot extract at low SNR.

  Fusion: "add" (default) multiplies the 4 MF tokens by a zero-initialized
  gate and adds them to the geometry tokens; "concat" appends them as 4
  separate tokens with a type embedding. The MF tokens are computed after
  geometry dropout, so they are always present.

6.4 Polarization tokens (polarization_features.py)

  Each detector records a different combination of the two polarizations:
  d_I = F+_I h+ + Fx_I hx, with h+ ∝ (1 + cos² ι)/2 and hx ∝ cos ι. Matching
  every detector with the same template gives one complex number per
  detector, z_I. Ratios cancel distance and orbital phase:

    z_I / z_J = [F+_I (1 + c²)/2 − i Fx_I c] / [F+_J (1 + c²)/2 − i Fx_J c],   c = cos ι

  so they depend only on sky position, polarization angle and inclination.

  Pass 1  template with the highest network SNR (chunked over templates,
          keeping only per-template peaks).
  Pass 2  full overlap series for that template; parabolic sub-sample peak
          refinement, linear interpolation of the complex value, heterodyne
          phase restored.
  Output  per pair (HL, HV, LV): log|z_I/z_J|, cos Δφ, sin Δφ, Δt [ms];
          per detector: asinh(SNR)                              = 15 features

  Requires --mf_tokens (uses the same bank). Verified against the analytic
  ratio: phase error 0.006 rad (median), amplitude scatter 1.3%.

6.5 Flow (flows.py, nflows)

  10 × [ ReversePermutation
         → MaskedPiecewiseRationalQuadraticAutoregressiveTransform
           (16 bins, linear tails, tail bound 5, 2 residual blocks,
            256 hidden units, context 288) ]
  base distribution N(0, I) on 11 dimensions

  Sizes are LeanNPE constructor defaults (flow_layers=10, flow_hidden=256,
  flow_bins=16), not stored in checkpoint args.

6.6 Parameter scaling (ParamScaler)

  Fixed invertible map physical ↔ [-1, 1]; nothing is fitted.

  Flow coordinate        Range                     Scale
  ────────────────────   ───────────────────────   ──────
  chirp mass (mc_q)      0.8 – 95 M☉               log
  mass ratio q (mc_q)    0.008 – 1                 linear
  luminosity_distance    dist_range (per model)    log
  ra                     0 – 2π                    linear, circular
  dec                    −π/2 – π/2                linear
  theta_jn               0 – π                     linear
  psi                    0 – π                     linear, circular
  phase                  0 – 2π                    linear, circular
  geocent_time           −1.6 – 1.6 s              linear
  a1, a2                 0 – 1                     linear

  mass_param = "mc_q" (production): the flow models (log Mc, q) on a box,
  and q ≤ 1 makes mass_1 ≥ mass_2 hold by construction. Physical interfaces
  always use (mass_1, mass_2). dist_range is a buffer stored in the state
  dict (BBH 80–5000, NSBH 15–1600, BNS 7–550, mixed 8–6000 Mpc).

  Sampling: z ~ N(0, I) → flow inverse → circular parameters wrapped
  exactly, others clamped → physical units.

6.7 Size

  Component                      BBH / mixed     NSBH / BNS
  ────────────────────────────   ────────────    ──────────
  conv stem                          199 k          199 k
  transformer                      1.33 M         1.33 M
  output projection                 967 k          967 k
  geometry branch                   141 k          141 k
  MF branch                         636 k            —
  polarization branch                68 k            —
  energy + PSD branches              13 k           13 k
  encoder total                    3.51 M         2.81 M
  flow                             6.21 M         6.21 M
  total                            9.72 M         9.02 M


7. TRAINING — experiments/train_lean_npe.py
===========================================

  Loss          mean NLL over all signals present: the encoder runs once per
                event, the flow once per rank present in the batch.
                --aux_mass 1.0 adds a SmoothL1 regression of the rank-0
                (Mc, q) from the encoder context (training only).
  Optimizer     AdamW, lr 3e-4, weight decay 1e-5, gradient clip 5
  Schedule      linear warmup 500 steps, cosine decay to 1% of peak
  Batch         128 events; 40 epochs (class models), 80 (mixed model)
  Data          RemixDataset, 12 loader workers, pinned memory

  Per epoch
    validation NLL     fixed Gaussian validation set, and a fixed real-noise
                       validation set when a noise bank is used
    diagnostics        on 1024 validation events × 128 posterior samples:
                       shufΔ    NLL rise when contexts are shuffled across
                                events (the encoder is being used)
                       dcorr    correlation of posterior median vs true d_L
                       dcov     distance 50/90% coverage
                       rail     spurious railing: samples pinned at a prior
                                bound whose truth is not near it
                       zc       E‖z‖²/D of the truth in base space (1 = calibrated)
                       covHi    mass/distance 90% coverage at high SNR
                       sbc      fraction of parameters passing SBC
                       corner   per-parameter error table
    basin probe        BBH models only: 6 fixed heavy-BBH injections that
                       detect a collapse to equal masses

  Checkpoint selection
    selection metric   mean of Gaussian and real-noise validation NLL
    calibration gate   spurious railing ≤ 0.10 (optional high-SNR coverage)
    best_model.pth     best metric among calibrated epochs (epochs passing
                       the basin probe rank first); best-NLL fallback until
                       a calibrated epoch exists
    also written       last_model.pth every epoch, epoch_XXXX.pth every
                       --ckpt_every epochs, history.json

  Options       --amp bf16 (encoder under autocast, flow fp32), --compile
                (torch.compile on the encoder), --profile_steps N
                (time data wait vs GPU step and exit)


8. CERTIFICATION — scripts/validate_checkpoint.py
=================================================

  Runs automatically after each training; writes analysis/ci/<model>/
  report.html and report.json. Gates:

    Gaussian shuffle ΔNLL > 5 nats
    Gaussian SBC KS p > 1e-3 for ≥ 9/11 parameters
    Gaussian spurious railing < 5%
    distance correlation > 0.5
    distance unbiased per source class (|bias| < 25%, 90% coverage > 0.80)
    no parameter effectively unmeasured (posterior/prior width < 0.85)
    chirp-mass width × SNR flat in SNR (ratio < 2)
    real-noise shuffle ΔNLL > 5 nats
    real-noise 90% coverage within ±0.07 (≤ 2 exceptions)
    real vs Gaussian NLL gap < 3 nats
    real GWTC events of the trained classes: run end to end, |t_c| < 0.1 s
      BBH:  GW150914, GW151226, GW170104, GW170608, GW170729, GW170814
      NSBH: GW200115, GW200105
      BNS:  GW170817, GW190425
    basin probe (BBH models)


9. INFERENCE — src/ahsd/inference/
==================================

  infer.py / pipeline.infer(event | strain | injection, event_type, rank)

  ┌ preprocessing.py
  │   real data: fetch from GWOSC (gwpy), highpass 15 Hz, ASD by median
  │   estimator (robust to the signal), whiten irfft(rfft(x)/ASD) on a long
  │   segment, trim 2 s edges, unit noise floor from an off-source region,
  │   4 s window centred on the trigger time; asd_bands from the measured
  │   ASDs. Simulated data: BilbyPreprocessor (as in training).
  │   A detector that is not observing is filled with unit white noise.
  ├ resolve_model: class model for event_type (CLASS_MODELS), else the
  │   mixed model; load_model() rebuilds LeanNPE from checkpoint args (cached)
  ├ sample_posterior(strain, rank, n_samples, asd_bands)
  ├ ood.py: Mahalanobis distance of the context to the training context
  │   cloud, calibrated against validation events (ood_stats.npz next to the
  │   checkpoint); combined with input-quality flags and railing into a
  │   HIGH / MEDIUM / LOW confidence verdict
  ├ gating.py: refinement gate from five indicators (confidence verdict,
  │   OOD percentile, measured bias region, posterior width, railing);
  │   strong indicators refine alone, two moderate ones refine together;
  │   bias grid from inference/assets/twin_grid.json (scripts/twin_grid.py)
  ├ priors.py: TrainingPrior — the prior the checkpoint was trained on for
  │   the event's class: per-class mass and spin bounds from the generator,
  │   distance range and shape from the dataset (recorded in checkpoint
  │   args). Single source for importance sampling and dynesty, including
  │   the waveform model (the generator's per class, zero tides) and the
  │   likelihood band: templates start where the lightest plausible chirp
  │   mass enters the 4 s segment (window_fmin), so long BNS/NSBH templates
  │   do not wrap and the likelihood sees the same band as the network
  ├ importance.py: importance sampling against the bilby likelihood,
  │   phase- and time-marginalized (bilby's time reference = data start
  │   time), w = L·π / q with π = TrainingPrior, symmetrized for the mass
  │   ordering; effective sample size reported
  ├ dynesty_bridge.py: full dynesty run with matched conventions (same PSDs,
  │   epoch, TrainingPrior support) for events flagged for refinement
  └ result.py: PosteriorResult — medians, credible intervals, correlations,
      distance-prior reweighting (uniform → d_L²), plots, bilby-compatible
      export, reproducibility record (checkpoint, git commit, settings)

  Overlaps: infer_overlapping(n_signals) runs infer() once per rank;
  PriorityNet (src/ahsd/core/priority_net.py, optional) reorders the results
  when a checkpoint exists.


10. MODELS, CHECKPOINTS AND COMPATIBILITY
=========================================

  Model                 Data              Distance       Encoder features
  ───────────────────   ───────────────   ────────────   ──────────────────────────────
  lean_npe_bbh_v3       dataset_bbh_v3    80–5000 Mpc    geometry + MF (BBH bank) + pol
  lean_npe_nsbh_v3      dataset_nsbh_v3   15–1600 Mpc    geometry
  lean_npe_bns_v3       dataset_bns_v3    7–550 Mpc      geometry
  lean_npe_v3 (mixed)   dataset_v3        8–6000 Mpc     geometry + MF (BBH bank) + pol

  All: coherent encoder, PSD conditioning, mc_q, delay_aug 0.5, aux_mass 1.0,
  geom_dropout 0.25, real_noise_prob 0.9, det_dropout 0.2.

  best_model.pth = {model_state_dict, args (training argparse namespace),
                    epoch, val_nll, diagnostics}
  args also records dataset_event_types and the dataset's distance_prior.

  Loading: LeanNPE is rebuilt from args at every load site (pipeline.py,
  validate_checkpoint.py, the scripts/). Every new LeanNPE constructor
  argument must be read from args at every load site, or older scripts fail
  on new checkpoints. Not in args: the flow sizes (constructor defaults) and
  dist_range (a state-dict buffer). The MF bank is loaded from assets by
  file name and is not stored in the checkpoint.


11. CLUSTER PIPELINE — scripts/run_pipeline.py, scripts/slurm/
==============================================================

  Run on the login node (compute nodes have no internet):

    python scripts/run_pipeline.py --regenerate

  1. prefetch the certification events into the shared gwpy cache
  2. per model: delete the old dataset → generate_parallel.sbatch (CPU node)
     → audit_dataset.sbatch (afterok) → train_lean_npe.sbatch (afterok,
     one full H100; certifies at the end)
  3. summary job (afterany, all trainings) → summarize_runs.py →
     analysis/RUN_SUMMARY.md

  Per-model flags are set in run_pipeline.MODELS (dataset, config, epochs,
  distance support, MF/polarization flags, generation node, seed).

  Logs: logs/gen_parallel-<job>.out, logs/audit-<job>.out,
  logs/train-<name>-<job>.out, model/<name>/train.log and validate.log,
  logs/pipeline.log, logs/summary-<job>.out.


12. THROUGHPUT
==============

